          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "In Perth’s prestige property landscape, the luxury off-the-plan and penthouse market is distinct. Because the buyer demographic consists heavily of affluent local downsizers from the Western Suburbs and riverfront enclaves, success hinges on deep local buyer networks, architectural appreciation, and refined display-suite capabilities.\n\nThe market leaders are divided into **dedicated project marketing agencies**, **prestige boutique brokerages**, and **integrated luxury developer-marketers**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Premier Project Marketing Agencies\n\n#### **Jones Realty & Projects**\n* **Market Position:** The benchmark for independent residential project marketing in Western Australia.\n* **Track Record:** Multi-year winner of REIWA’s *Top Office for Residential Project Marketing* and *Top Salesperson* awards (led by Steve and Nicole Jones).\n* **Focus:** High-end architectural developments, boutique riverfront residences, and luxury multi-residential projects across South Perth, Applecross, and the Western Suburbs (e.g., *Ninety Seven South Perth*, *Astoria Applecross*). They provide end-to-end services—from floorplan design optimization to display suite execution and settlement management.\n\n#### **Ray White Projects WA (in alignment with Ray White Dalkeith | Claremont)**\n* **Market Position:** The nexus between elite residential sales and off-the-plan project delivery.\n* **Key Figure:** **Vivien Yap**, widely regarded as Perth’s highest-profile luxury property agent.\n* **Focus:** When developers release ultra-prime architectural projects or penthouses in the Golden Triangle (Cottesloe, Nedlands, Dalkeith, Claremont, City Beach), this group is frequently engaged. They leverage an unmatched database of high-net-worth local and overseas buyers looking to downsize from substantial family estates into luxury penthouses.\n\n#### **PRD Real Estate Perth**\n* **Market Position:** Major player for landmark, high-density, and five-star branded developments.\n* **Key Figure:** **Angus Murray**.\n* **Focus:** Specializes in scale, waterfront, and inner-city architectural projects. Their portfolio includes marketing some of Perth's most prominent off-the-plan addresses, such as *The Towers at Elizabeth Quay* (anchored by The Ritz-Carlton) and *NV Apartments*.\n\n#### **Boutique Property and Advisory (BPA)**\n* **Market Position:** Specialized boutique advisory focusing purely on prestige off-the-plan developments and sky homes.\n* **Key Figure:** **Stephen Vitale**.\n* **Focus:** Highly active in the Western Suburbs and coastal luxury corridors (e.g., North Fremantle, Cottesloe, Subiaco). They are known for collaborating directly with architects during the conceptual stage to ensure floor plates and penthouse specifications match ultra-prime buyer demands.\n\n#### **Limnios Property Group**\n* **Market Position:** WA’s longest-running apartment project marketing firm.\n* **Focus:** Having operated since the early 1990s, Limnios has delivered over $3.5 billion in off-the-plan apartment sales. While they handle high-density metro projects, they have a substantial legacy in marketing premium riverfront and inner-city penthouses.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Major Integrated Luxury Developers (Internal Project Marketing)\n\nIn Perth, several of the most architecturally ambitious penthouses and luxury developments are marketed and sold directly by the developers’ in-house project sales teams:\n\n* **Blackburne:** Founded by Paul Blackburne, this group is the market benchmark for multi-million-dollar penthouse sales in Western Australia. Blackburne sets the state's record prices for penthouses (notably across *One Subiaco*, *The Grove* in Cottesloe/Claremont, *Eclipse South Perth*, and *Ocean Grand* in City Beach), regularly commanding sales between $15M and $25M+. Their internal marketing machines and luxury display pavilions set the standard in Perth.\n* **Celsius Property Group:** Led by Richard Pappas, Celsius blends development management with an internal project sales arm. They specialize in design-led, medium-density luxury developments crafted by leading architectural studios (e.g., Rothelowman, MJA Studio) in affluent pockets like Subiaco, North Perth, and Shenton Park.\n* **Edge Visionary Living:** Prominent developer of sculptural, architecturally bold riverfront and coastal developments (frequently collaborating with Hillam Architects). They maintain specialized sales consultants dedicated exclusively to their high-end apartment and penthouse stock.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Global Commercial Consultancies\n\n* **Colliers Residential WA:** The local residential arm of the global real estate group. They are typically enlisted for large-scale, institutional-grade master-planned mixed-use precincts, leveraging a global cross-border network for capital and off-shore buyers.\n\n---\n\n### Key Takeaways for Developers & Buyers\n* **For Boutique Western Suburbs/River Penthouses ($3M–$15M+):** **Jones Realty & Projects**, **Ray White Projects (Vivien Yap)**, and **Boutique Property and Advisory** are the standard selections for project marketing due to their qualified local downsizer databases.\n* **For Landmark High-Rise & Mixed-Use Precincts:** **PRD Perth** and **Colliers** provide the operational scale, investor channels, and project infrastructure required for high unit counts.",
